# Section titles stay small — enlarge cards only

Hard rule for diana’s dashboard (`/Users/diana/my-dashboard`) vision collage / overview-era days.

## Never

- Enlarge **section** titles (`.vision-tile-title`, zone heads, collage section names)
- “Glance readability” patches that bump **both** section titles and card captions together
- Shared font-size variables / clamps that apply to `.vision-tile-title` and polaroid/card text
- Zoom styles that make section titles huge (`clamp(32px…52px)`, `clamp(40px…56px)`, `36px`, or larger)
- A different title recipe in collage overview vs section zoom (size, foil, carve, filter)
- Re-bumping section titles after Diana already reverted them

## Always

1. **Section titles** stay at the approved small size in **both** collage overview and section zoom:
   - `clamp(22px, 2.6vw, 34px)` — same foil / carve / filter in both views
2. **Only** enlarge card/task text: `.vision-polaroid span`, `.vision-shot-card span`, `.vision-habit-title`, task labels
3. When asked to make collage text more glanceable, touch **card** rules only — leave `.vision-tile-title` alone
4. Edit `everything.html` (+ `dashboard-current.css` foil size lock) — do not fork zoom to a second size
5. Style block `vision-collage-glance-type-v2` / `sep6-gold-foil-titles-lock` lock section titles small and cards larger — do not revert to v1’s dual bump or a zoom-only 36px

## If section titles look huge again — or overview ≠ zoom

Fix immediately (same clamp + foil in both views). Do not ask permission. Do not “improve readability” by enlarging sections.
